      },
      "message": "fix(import): load a STEP closed shell that meshes open as an incomplete model\n\nA closed shell whose mesh has a real gap was refused at import (#1576),\nso the part could not be viewed or set up. The model import now lands it\nincomplete: fidelity unknown (the #1056 sentinel, which rides every\nchord path) with its hole named in a new MeshOpen component, saved as\nthe entity key mesh_open. Every operation on it, a fixture made from it\nand the program verdict are refused at the post naming the hole; the\nmodel page, import status and MCP/script facts say \"Incomplete\". The\nhole rides UpdateModel and DeleteEntity undo and the project file; a\nmesh_open without the mark is corrupt. Fixture, tool-body and mesh-only\nloaders still refuse the file by name.\n\nFixes #1610\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
